 "about_text": "Brand Library & Art Center occupies the restored 1904 Miradero mansion, the former Glendale estate of civic figure Leslie C. Brand, whose Indo-Islamic-styled house was donated to the city upon his death in 1925 and converted into a public library that opened in 1956. A 1969 addition added a gallery and recital hall, and the whole complex was renovated and reopened in 2014. Operated as a branch of the City of Glendale Library, Arts & Culture Department, it combines a specialized visual-arts and music library collection with rotating exhibitions, concerts, dance performances, lectures and community arts programs, serving as a cultural and historic landmark at the base of the Verdugo Mountains.",
